## Project Structure

```text
terraform/
├── main.tf            # Locals sanitization logic, IAM User, and IAM Role resources
├── variables.tf       # Input variable definitions with custom validation rules
├── terraform.tfvars   # Environment-specific variable assignments
├── outputs.tf         # Exported resource names and applied IAM user tags
└── provider.tf        # AWS provider configuration
Implementation Details
1. Input Variables & Validation (variables.tf)
KKE_PROJECT: Enforces a non-empty string using length(trimspace(var.KKE_PROJECT)) > 0.

KKE_TEAM: Enforces alphanumeric characters, dashes, or underscores via regex("^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$", var.KKE_TEAM).

KKE_ENVIRONMENT: Specifies the target deployment environment (dev).

2. Sanitization & Tagging (main.tf)
Sanitization: Converts KKE_PROJECT and KKE_TEAM to lowercase and replaces any non-alphanumeric character (excluding -) with - using replace(lower(...), "/[^a-z0-9-]/", "-").

Prefix Construction: Combines sanitized values into local.name_prefix (devops-dev-team).

Governance Tags: Applies Project, Team, ManagedBy = "Terraform", and Env to both resources, merging RoleType = "EC2" onto aws_iam_role.kke_role.

3. Outputs (outputs.tf)
Output Name	Description	Resolved Value
kke_user_name	Name of the created IAM user	devops-dev-team-user
kke_role_name	Name of the created IAM role	devops-dev-team-role
kke_tags_applied	Tags applied to the IAM user	{ Env = "dev", ManagedBy = "Terraform", Project = "devops", Team = "dev-team" }
Deployment & Verification
Bash
# Initialize, validate, and apply configuration
terraform init
terraform validate
terraform apply -auto-approve

# Verify zero configuration drift
terraform plan

# Verify live AWS IAM resources and tags
aws iam get-user --user-name devops-dev-team-user
aws iam list-user-tags --user-name devops-dev-team-user
aws iam get-role --role-name devops-dev-team-role
aws iam list-role-tags --role-name devops-dev-team-role

